  "body": "Follows #2904 (merged). Part 2 of #917.\n\n## What changed\n\n- The tool coordinate-system reader, the length-unit reader and the STEP syntax locator move from `crates/app/src/geometry/import/` to `camcraft-geometry`:\n  - `camcraft_geometry::step_csys` (types and `read_tool_csys(text)`) and `step_csys_read` (the reader).\n  - `camcraft_geometry::step_units` (`length_unit_mm`).\n  - `camcraft_geometry::step_diag` (`locate`; each DATA record is now checked with the solidcore Part 21 parser).\n- The readers use `camcraft_kernel::p21`. This is a one-line re-export of `solidcore_step::p21`. The solidcore pin stays in the kernel manifest only. There is no new edge between our crates.\n- The app keeps `step_csys.rs` as a thin wrapper: the nesting scan, the empty and UTF-8 checks, and the map to `ImportError`. It re-exports the types, so the callers (`tool_body*`, MCP) do not change.\n- `step_depth` code does not change. It stays the nesting law in front of every read. Its documents now say why.\n- `ruststep` is removed from `crates/app/Cargo.toml`. `Cargo.lock` loses only the app edge. The root pin and the kernel dev-dependencies stay for part 3 (#2790).\n- In the browser build (wasm32), `read_tool_csys` refuses by name, as the model import already does.\n- Review fix: the unit reader refuses a file that has a length unit when no unit context states a length unit (see \"Readings\").\n\n## Readings (decisions in `docs/decisions/2789-step-readers-solidcore.md`)\n\n- An entity id that is defined two times: the reader refuses the file by name. ruststep kept the last definition and the new parser keeps the first. No tracked fixture has a duplicate id.\n- A file with no DATA section: the reader refuses it with the old text \"file has no DATA section\".\n- Several DATA sections: the reader reads them as one (ISO 10303-21 edition 3). The old reader read only the first.\n- A syntax error of the tool-body read has the wording of the model import now (the entity, its line and its text).\n- The nesting limit: the parser has its own cap of 64. But it accepts an empty innermost `()` one level past that cap. The scan refuses that record. Both sides are pinned.\n- A length unit that no unit context states: the read is refused by name. The parser maps short names such as `A2PL3D` and `LNGUNT`, but not the short forms of `GLOBAL_UNIT_ASSIGNED_CONTEXT` and `SI_UNIT`. Thus a short-name tool file gave a CIP but no unit context, and the reader used 1 mm per unit. The refusal applies when the file has one of these records:\n  - a `LENGTH_UNIT`;\n  - an `SI_UNIT` of the metre;\n  - a `CONVERSION_BASED_UNIT` over a `LENGTH_MEASURE_WITH_UNIT`.\n  The refusal text is \"length unit #N is in the file, but no GLOBAL_UNIT_ASSIGNED_CONTEXT states a length unit ...\". A file with no unit record keeps 1 mm per unit, as the ruststep reader did. The reader does not guess the two short names: no public source in the repository or in the solidcore checkout states them.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/geometry/tests/step_csys_read.rs` (new, 11): `the_fixture_reads_through_the_part_21_parser`, `an_entity_id_defined_twice_is_refused_by_name`, `a_file_with_no_data_section_is_refused_by_its_old_text`, `several_data_sections_are_read_as_one`, `a_syntax_error_names_the_entity_and_its_line`, `the_parser_alone_takes_an_empty_list_one_past_its_depth_cap`, `corrupt_input_is_a_clean_error_never_a_panic`, and for the units:\n  - `a_short_name_tool_file_in_inches_or_metres_is_refused_by_name`;\n  - `a_short_name_tool_file_with_a_long_unit_context_reads_at_its_scale` (inch 25.4, metre 1000, millimetre 1);\n  - `a_long_name_tool_file_in_inches_reads_at_twenty_five_point_four`;\n  - `a_tool_file_with_no_unit_record_keeps_millimetres`.\n- `crates/geometry/tests/step_units.rs` (new, 6): the 4 in-file tests of the app, moved, `a_unit_that_converts_to_itself_is_refused_at_the_chain_cap`, and `a_length_unit_that_no_context_states_is_refused_by_name` (an angle-only file still keeps millimetres).\n- `crates/geometry/tests/step_diag.rs` (new, 4): the locator wording (\"cannot be parsed\", \"no DATA section found\", \"is never closed\") and the records that pass.\n- `crates/app/tests/step_nesting.rs`: new `an_empty_list_one_past_the_cap_is_refused_by_the_scan`.\n- Not changed and green: `tool_csys` (11), `step_nesting` (9), `import` (26), `import_step_closed_shell` (6), `tool_body` (12), `tool_body_assembly` (5), `tool_body_view` (7), `mcp_tool_body` (5), geometry `step_metre_unit` (1).\n- The `#[test]` count goes up by 18: 22 tests are added (4 of them moved from the app) and 4 app unit tests are removed.\n\n## Gate\n\nFirst head (a29d79a65 merged with main), run before the review:\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-geometry --test step_units --test step_csys_read --test step_diag --test step_metre_unit`: 17 passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test tool_csys --test step_nesting --test import --test tool_body --test tool_body_assembly --test tool_body_view --test mcp_tool_body --test import_step_closed_shell`: 81 passed.\n- `cargo check -p camcraft-geometry --target wasm32-unknown-unknown`: builds (one old warning in `step.rs`, not from this PR).\n\nReview fix (head 4b694c7c7, after `git merge origin/main`):\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-geometry --test step_units --test step_csys_read --test step_diag`: 21 passed.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test tool_csys --test step_nesting --test tool_body --test mcp_tool_body`: 37 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-kernel -p camcraft-geometry -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The batch tier and the heavy lanes. The model-import suites outside the lists above were not run. `import`, `tool_body_assembly`, `tool_body_view`, `import_step_closed_shell` and `step_metre_unit` were not run again on the review-fix head.\n- The full browser build (`web/build-app-wasm.sh`). Only the geometry crate was checked for wasm32, and only on the first head.\n- Real vendor tool files with string escapes (`\\X2\\...`). The new parser decodes them; ruststep did not. No fixture has them.\n- Real short-name tool files: the pins use hand-made text.\n\n## Follow-up\n\n- #2919: the model import has the same unit gap in the kernel's `length_units`. That is a separate PR.\n\nChangelog: The tool-body STEP reader refuses a file in which an entity id is defined two times, refuses a file whose length unit no unit context states, and reads all DATA sections of a file.\n\nRefs #917\n\nFixes #2789\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
